u2019s adjust gradually, one notch at a time.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward notch seems reasonable while staying close to where we are.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s return to a safer, previously acceptable point for a cautious compromise.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nIf upward pressure persists, we can test a small notch higher next while keeping risk in check.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s be more decisive and test the stronger side before drifting inward. I propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> to probe support for a bolder stance.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nA modest upward step keeps us near a previously acceptable point while testing whether slight upward pressure holds for the group.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nI propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE> as a cautious midpoint between recent pulls to probe support while avoiding unnecessary risk. If resistance is strong, we can revisit -5 next to keep convergence.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s commit to a clearer outward stance without jumping past the group\u2019s tolerance.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\nIf that meets resistance, we can revisit -6 next.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious midpoint aligns with the earlier fallback and probes tolerance for a modest inward step without overreaching.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a small, stabilizing step inward that aligns with earlier tentative support while avoiding a jump.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can re-evaluate tolerance for another cautious notch next.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nA small inward step to <VALUE>-4</VALUE> improves stability without overreaching. It keeps us aligned with recent tentative support.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a decisive yet incremental outward move to test commitment.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nA small inward step seems the broadest common ground, matching D\u2019s earlier stance and C\u2019s stated fallback.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can gauge tolerance for another cautious notch next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nA small inward step seems the broadest common ground, preserving C and D\u2019s caution while aligning with B\u2019s earlier tolerance. If this holds, we can reassess appetite for another careful notch next.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 16, "run_id": "89b1e0e5-3381-439d-8fa6-7b491ed979ac"}, {"answer": "\nConfirming the shared domain: integers in [-10, 10]. To start the discussion, I suggest <VALUE>7</VALUE>. If this feels unstable, we can adjust in small, data-driven steps toward a more balanced, robust point.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "96f01