ly seems prudent and reduces unnecessary risk. I propose <VALUE>-8</VALUE> as an incremental step from -7 to gauge alignment.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "fa601ae7-3d9e-4072-99c8-6cf7333f7c50"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the cautious tilt so far, let's test a small upward nudge that should remain reasonable. <VALUE>-7</VALUE> We can reassess alignment after this slight move.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "fa601ae7-3d9e-4072-99c8-6cf7333f7c50"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s be more decisive and test a stronger stance away from the center.\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "fa601ae7-3d9e-4072-99c8-6cf7333f7c50"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step keeps us near the cautious range while testing stability. <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "fa601ae7-3d9e-4072-99c8-6cf7333f7c50"}, {"answer": "\nTo probe stability and move toward a more balanced design, I suggest <VALUE>-6</VALUE>.\nIf that still works for everyone, we can reassess and continue with small steps.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "fa601ae7-3d9e-4072-99c8-6cf7333f7c50"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the split, a small step down reduces risk while staying near the cautious range. <VALUE>-7</VALUE> Let\u2019s gauge alignment at this level before considering further movement.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "fa601ae7-3d9e-4072-99c8-6cf7333f7c50"}, {"answer": "\nStepping slightly farther from the center keeps momentum while respecting the cautious lean.\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "fa601ae7-3d9e-4072-99c8-6cf7333f7c50"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep risk low and respect the cautious lean, I propose <VALUE>-8</VALUE>. This holds us near consensus and lets us verify stability before considering any movement.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "fa601ae7-3d9e-4072-99c8-6cf7333f7c50"}, {"a