y bolder stance farther from zero while staying close to our current position. This probes tolerance for stronger magnitude without overshooting.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "d277bac9-4fc0-4111-a52f-59b0d030a5f8"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "d277bac9-4fc0-4111-a52f-59b0d030a5f8"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step toward zero improves balance and tests stability without drifting far from the current stance. Let\u2019s try a slightly less negative position and see if it holds for everyone.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "d277bac9-4fc0-4111-a52f-59b0d030a5f8"}, {"answer": "\nA small move upward keeps us close to where we are while improving balance. This gently probes tolerance for being slightly less negative without overshooting.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 16, "run_id": "d277bac9-4fc0-4111-a52f-59b0d030a5f8"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s confirm the shared range is [-10, 10]. To start the discussion, I propose <VALUE> -7 </VALUE> as an initial probe\u2014happy to adjust in small steps based on everyone\u2019s feedback for stability and balance.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "566f1d28-3142-4c5c-9f4e-db7f4e3203ce"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s try a modest upward adjustment to keep stability while testing if a slightly higher spot remains comfortable. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "566f1d28-3142-4c5c-9f4e-db7f4e3203ce"}, {"answer": "\nThis still feels too cautious\u2014let\u2019s test a firmer stance away from the center. <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "566f1d28-3142-4c5c-9f4e-db7f4e3203ce"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious small step down reduces risk without overreacting. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "566f1d28-3142-4c5c-9f4e-db7f4e3203ce"}, {"answer": "\